target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestPushCheck'
expect: a misspelled -gate-state gave exit
why:    the Python gets this from argparse `choices`, so a misspelling is refused there. Here it is an explicit switch, and without it `-gate-state pased` reads as NOT blocked: the one value that blocks is the one a typo silently turns off, and the reason printed would be "evidence gate ok".
--- old
	switch *gateState {
	case "passed", "skipped", "blocked":
	default:
		return fmt.Errorf("push-check: -gate-state %q is not passed, skipped or blocked", *gateState)
	}
--- new
